 this crazy stuff by the way originates  from inside Trump's White House Donald  Trump is not well as a whole the country  has appeared to be unwilling to address  this even as a possibility this is  understandable  we have gradually grown as a society to  understand the nature of mental illness  physically based or otherwise even in my  childhood this was a subject of fear and  confusion and blame and now finally we  are sympathetic but for 50 years we have  also asked our mental health  professionals not to diagnose our  presidential want to B's from afar  unfortunately this is like saying that  you cannot call it a forest fire unless  you work for the National Park Service  at the specific forest and you have  personally been singed by the fire our  refusal out of sympathy and fairness to  call some kind of paranoid delusion some  kind of paranoid delusion could destroy  this country the latest Quinnipiac poll  asked recipients to give a description  of Trump using the first word that came  into their heads not multiple-choice  just give me the word that best  describes him 46 different words were  given five times or more the leaders  were idiot incompetent liar leader  unqualified president strong businessman  ignorant egotistical [ __ ] just  missing the top 10 tied with stupid  arrogant trying excellent thoughtful  word they're trying bully business  narcissists successful disgusting great  clown dishonest racist American bigot  good money smart buffoon conman crazy  different disaster rich despicable  dictator aggressive blowhard decisive  embarrassment evil greedy in experienced  mental negotiator patriotism only three  words that even hint at psychiatric  issues quote crazy quote mental and  quote narcissist use just a combined of  23 times from a total of 527 people  Trump's aides spend 48 hours violently  insisting James Comey spiring had  nothing to do with Russia he then gives  an interview and says of course he was  thinking about Russia destroying the  argument and his aides he hinted a  secret taping system in the White House  something even Richard  Nixon hid for more than four years he  uses the phrase priming the pump about  the economy and then claims he just made  the phrase up and he asks the  interviewer do you like it even though  there is documentary evidence that prime  the pump has been used to describe  government action to energize an economy  since at least 1933 and he thinks he  just coined it last week but nobody will  call him crazy that one little quote  from the Washington Post might be a  harbinger of increased belief among his  supporters that Trump is dangerously  unstable one GOP figure close to the  White House mused privately about  whether Trump was in the grip of some  kind of paranoid delusion but they can't  admit that if you supported a candidate  and he was elected president and it  turned out you were wrong and all your  opponents were right and he really was  crazy would you admit it nevertheless it  might be leaking out over the sides in  the Quinnipiac poll On February 7th 88  percent of Republicans said they  approved Trump 75 percent said they  strongly approved Trump in the  Quinnipiac poll on May 10th 82 percent  of Republicans said they approved Trump  but only 63 percent still said they  strongly approved Trump same thing in an  NBC poll 90 percent Republican approval  On February 5th 67 percent strong  approval 88 percent Republican approve  on May 11th no change just 54 percent  strong approval to polls in which in  three months about 20% of Trump's  Republican support has sunk from strong  approval to just regular approval  maybe the Trump thing is metal health'  the chaos of his administration Russia  whatever is slowly creeping into the  awareness even of the Republicans and  they had better figure it out fast  because there is also something new and  I don't think this has been reported  anywhere else that suggests what happens  when you do not act quickly enough 